{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/relativeY"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default-x and default-y attributes change the computation of the default position. For most elements, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"origin is changed relative to the left-hand side of the note or the musical position within the bar (x) and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the top line of the staff (y).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the following elements, the default-x value changes the origin relative to the start of the current"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measure:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"note - figured-bass - harmony - link - directive - measure-numbering - all descendants of the part-list"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element - all children of the direction-type element"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This origin is from the start of the entire measure, at either the left barline or the start of the system.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the default-x attribute is used within a child element of the part-name-display, part-abbreviation-","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display, group-name-display, or group-abbreviation-display elements, it changes the origin relative to the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of the first measure on the system. These values are used when the current measure or a succeeding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measure starts a new system. The same change of origin is used for the group-symbol element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the note, figured-bass, and harmony elements, the default-x value is considered to have adjusted the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"musical position within the bar for its descendant elements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since the credit-words and credit-image elements are not related to a measure, in these cases the default-x"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and default-y attributes adjust the origin relative to the bottom left-hand corner of the specified page."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The relative-x and relative-y attributes change the position relative to the default position, either as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"computed by the individual program, or as overridden by the default-x and default-y attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive x is right, negative x is left; positive y is up, negative y is down. All units are in tenths of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interline space. For stems, positive relative-y lengthens a stem while negative relative-y shortens it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default-x and default-y position attributes provide higher-resolution positioning data than related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features such as the placement attribute and the offset element. Applications reading a MusicXML file that can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understand both features should generally rely on the default-x and default-y attributes for their greater"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accuracy. For the relative-x and relative-y attributes, the offset element, placement attribute, and directive"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute provide context for the relative position information, so the two features should be interpreted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"together."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As elsewhere in the MusicXML format, tenths are the global tenths defined by the scaling element, not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local tenths of a staff resized by the staff-size element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLPosition","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"identifier"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","title":"Swift.Escapable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/defaultY":{"title":"defaultY","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultY","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/defaulty","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/defaultY","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The default vertical position, in tenths, changing the computation of the default position relative to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"top line of the staff."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/Equatable-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"title":"Equatable Implementations","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition\/Equatable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition\/equatable-implementations"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition/init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLPosition"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"init(defaultX:defaultY:relativeX:relativeY:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","id